    {
      "name": "WRL_ON",
      "label": "WRL_ON (GPIO23)",
      "codeName": "WRL_ON",
      "capabilities": [],
      "notes": "WiFi/BT radio (Raspberry Pi RM2 / CYW43439) power-enable line (WRL_ON) - dedicated radio control signal, not general purpose. Confirmed via this board's own pins_arduino.h comment \"// WiFi power GPIO\" + official product listing confirming a Raspberry Pi Radio Module 2 (RM2, CYW43439-based) WiFi/Bluetooth radio, matching the same dedicated-enable-line pattern documented for other RM2-equipped boards in this repo (e.g. sparkfun_thingplusrp2350)."
    },
    {
      "name": "GPIO26",
      "label": "GPIO26 (Led Neopixel)",
      "codeName": "26",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_neopixel"
      ],
      "notes": "Onboard WS2812 addressable RGB LED (PIN_NEOPIXEL/NUM_NEOPIXEL=1 in this board's own pins_arduino.h; no D26 alias otherwise exists since PIN_NEOPIXEL is a bare #define). Confirmed via the official raspberrypi/pico-sdk board header boards/soldered_nula_max_rp2350.h (PICO_DEFAULT_WS2812_PIN 26) and soldered.com's own product listing (\"WS2812 RGB LED\").\nCheck if available on board"
    },
    {
      "name": "USER_BTN",
      "label": "GPIO27 (Button)",
      "codeName": "USER_BTN",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_input",
        "button"
      ],
      "notes": "Onboard USER button (USER_BTN alias in this board's own pins_arduino.h). Confirmed via the official raspberrypi/pico-sdk board header boards/soldered_nula_max_rp2350.h (SOLDERED_NULA_MAX_RP2350_USER_BTN 27) and soldered.com's own product listing (\"RESET, BOOTSEL, and USER buttons\"). digital_output/pwm_output deliberately omitted - no vendor source confirms driving this line as output is safe, matching this repo's conservative precedent for board user-buttons (e.g. pimoroni_pico_plus_2w GPIO45)."
    },
